### Top-ups (FR-P-4, M7 part 2). Razorpay TEST MODE only, fake test data only.
# Prerequisites: core-app running with the local profile and RAZORPAY_* test keys in .env; a token for customer1
# from auth.http; customer1 has a wallet (kyc.http, minimum KYC is enough: MIN wallets may add up to ₹10,000).
# To actually pay: open http://localhost:8080/checkout.html (local profile only), paste the token and the top-up
# ID from the create response, click "Pay existing top-up", pay with UPI success@razorpay. The signed
# payment.captured webhook credits the wallet. Full end-to-end steps (tunnel, webhook, SQL): docs/e2e-razorpay.md.

### customer1: create a ₹500 top-up -> 201 {status PENDING, gatewayOrderId "order_...", keyId "rzp_test_..."}
# Run again unchanged -> the same 201 body with Idempotent-Replayed: true, and no second Razorpay order.
# Change the amount and run again with the same key -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 0b9a3c1e-7d2f-4e6a-8c5b-1f2e3d4c5b01
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "500.00"}

> {% client.global.set("topup_id", response.body.id); %}

### customer1: read it back -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/topups/{{topup_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer2: someone else's top-up -> 404 NOT_FOUND (same as an unknown ID)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/topups/{{topup_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2_token}}

### Above the monthly load (MIN wallet: ₹10,000) -> 422 LIMIT_EXCEEDED, no Razorpay order
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 0b9a3c1e-7d2f-4e6a-8c5b-1f2e3d4c5b02
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "10000.01"}

### Below the minimum -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 0b9a3c1e-7d2f-4e6a-8c5b-1f2e3d4c5b03
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "0.50"}

### Without Idempotency-Key -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{api}}/api/v1/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": "500.00"}
